cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "AetherZ3Omega: Honest Formalization Workspace for the Riemann Hypothesis Skeleton"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amry"
    given-names: "Muhammad Aidil"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9718-9710"
    affiliation: "Sovereign Orchestrator Project"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
type: "software"
license: "MIT"
repository: "https://github.com/aidilamrym-ops/riemann-hypothesis-formalization"
url: "https://github.com/aidilamrym-ops/riemann-hypothesis-formalization"
description: |
  Lean 4 (v4.33.1) formalization workspace for the Riemann Hypothesis skeleton.
  62/62 modules in lean4/AetherZ3Omega/Riemann kernel-compile from source with
  0 sorrys and one explicitly open postulate (AetherZ3Omega.riemann_hypothesis).
  RH and the Hilbert-Polia spectral correspondence remain OPEN; master theorems
  are re-framed honestly as conditional/consistency statements. Z3 SMT batches
  provide auxiliary consistency checks.
keywords:
  - "Riemann Hypothesis"
  - "Formal Verification"
  - "Lean 4"
  - "Z3 SMT"
  - "Spectral Rigidity"
  - "Entropy-Energy Coupling"
  - "Millennium Prize Problems"
